    "narrative": "LawDog enters May 14th with a balanced, if cautious, offensive outlook, headlined by the daily efficiency leader **Lawrence Butler** (72.20). Despite his projected seventh-spot placement, **Lawrence Butler** is a must-start today against McGreevy; the favorable park and pitching matchup provide the highest ceiling on our roster. **Will Smith** (64.10) and **Masyn Winn** (60.86) also project as strong starts, with **Masyn Winn** benefiting significantly from a high-park-factor environment and a favorable matchup against the left-handed Jacob Lopez. We are cautiously deploying **Brendan Donovan** (59.46) at the top of the lineup, where his platoon advantage against Burrows and leadoff positioning effectively mitigate his moderate base projection, keeping him just shy of the elite tier but firmly in our \"Strong\" category.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult decision at the margins, ultimately benching **Drew Gilbert** (36.02) in favor of our active starters. While **Drew Gilbert** offers intrigue, the combination of a daunting matchup against Emmet Sheehan and an assumed eighth-spot in the order dragged his efficiency well below our 40-point floor. Meanwhile, our heavy reliance on **Luis Arraez** (46.02), **Matt Chapman** (43.58), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.15) against Emmet Sheehan remains a point of concern; their scores are heavily suppressed by the SP\u2019s 3.16 xERA. We must also monitor the status of **Bryson Stott** (44.98), whose value is severely capped by a negative platoon split against the left-handed Ranger Suarez. With **Cal Raleigh** currently on the IL, we are holding firm with our current configuration, keeping **Wenceel Perez** on the bench to preserve game caps, as his efficiency failed to clear the 40-point barrier due to a unfavorable matchup against McLean.",
